From 27204f725cd10160d2da3c3f1c0d3b7f28442512 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:26:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Profiling: sections reported to the tracing profilers
 (markers, ranges)

A tracing profiler (Nsight Systems, the profilers of ROCm...) shows on a
time line the ranges that a program declares through an annotation library
(NVTX, roctx): declared as ranges, the timed sections give the context of
the kernels of a GPU. `setProfilingMarkers` sets two functions called at
the beginning, with its name, and at the end of each active section (none
by default, shared by all the contexts, as the synchronization function).
MGIS does not depend on any annotation library: the caller gives the
functions.

The range of a section is the interval measured by its timer: the
synchronization of the beginning of a section is now made before its node
is pushed in the profiling tree, which does not change the measured time
(the clock is read after both, as before). A section keeps the function
reporting its end: a section which began before the markers were set is
not reported.

A `ProfilingRange` object declares a range only reported by these
functions, neither timed nor added to the profiling tree (time steps,
iterations, whose names change at each call). Its name may be given by a
function, only called if the range is reported.

Tests (calls in order, nesting, inactive and forced sections, markers
changed while sections are open, unchanged profiling tree) and
documentation.
