+# Profiling sections in tracing profilers
+
+`setProfilingMarkers` sets two functions called at the beginning, with
+its name, and at the end of each active profiling section, for instance
+to declare the sections as ranges of an annotation library (`NVTX`,
+`roctx`, ...), which a tracing profiler shows on a time line.
+`getProfilingMarkers` returns these functions. A `ProfilingRange` object
+declares a range only reported by these functions, which is neither
+timed nor added to the profiling tree (a time step, an iteration). See
+the [profiling](profiling.html) page.
+
